# This file makes GitHub show a "Cite this repository" button in the sidebar,
# and Zenodo reads it when it archives a release.
#
# After Zenodo gives you a DOI, uncomment the `doi:` lines below and paste it in.
# Use the concept DOI, the one Zenodo says always resolves to the latest version,
# not the version-specific one.

cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "The GDPR Constellation: a compliance star map"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Sanchez-Villa"
    given-names: "Maria Fernanda"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/FernandaSVilla/GDPR-knowledge-constellation"
url: "https://fernandasvilla.github.io/GDPR-knowledge-constellation/"
abstract: >
  An interactive self-assessment tool covering 45 practical obligations under
  Regulation (EU) 2016/679, arranged as nine constellations from lawful basis to
  international transfers. Each obligation is cited to paragraph level, tagged by
  source (regulation text, CJEU case law or supervisory guidance), and mapped to
  the evidence a supervisory authority would expect together with its statutory
  maximum tier under Art. 83. Users assess their position, the tool computes
  maturity by domain, flags open 4 per cent tier exposure, and exports a
  prioritised gap report. Includes a study mode with recall questions. Built as a
  single self-contained HTML page with no backend; assessment data stays in the
  browser.
keywords:
  - GDPR
  - data protection
  - privacy
  - regulatory compliance
  - self-assessment
  - legal design
  - compliance maturity
